# Copy to `.env.development.local` (or `.env.local`) to run `npm run dev` against a real chain —
# `.env*` is gitignored repo-wide except this template, same convention as the root `.env.example`.
# Vite never loads `.env.example` itself; `vite build` (production mode) loads neither file, which
# is why a production build with nothing configured renders "not configured" rather than this data.
#
# UNLIKE THE ROOT `.env.example`, NOTHING BELOW IS A PLACEHOLDER. A public testnet RPC and a real,
# already-deployed vault address — there is nothing secret to fill in.
#
# THIS IS THE ONE LIVE-READ PATH THIS REPOSITORY CAN PROVE TODAY. Nothing from this repository is
# deployed on Arc mainnet (chain 5042) yet — contracts/config/arc-mainnet.json's own `status` field
# says so in as many words. Base Sepolia is: `contracts/config/deployments/base-sepolia.json`'s
# `smokeVault` ran the full ten-phase lifecycle and was re-read independently on-chain as recently
# as 2026-09-10 (totalShares 5e18, navWad 5e18, idleUsdc 5e6, holderCount 2) — and independently
# again while building this change (2026-09-19): navWad and totalShares unchanged, an ACTIVE
# proposal (#11, type Rebalance) present with real deadlines, decoded correctly end to end.
#
# `test/csp.test.mjs`'s "connect-src names the SAME origin VITE_RPC_URL actually resolves to..."
# test reads VITE_RPC_URL out of THIS file (the one guaranteed to be committed) and asserts it
# appears in public/_headers' connect-src — change one, change the other, in the same commit.
#
# VITE_VAULT_NAME IS OPTIONAL AND LEFT UNSET HERE ON PURPOSE. The vault this file points at is a
# generic Base Sepolia smoke-test fixture — it is not the v1 mainnet vault, and giving it the
# name "cirBTC Vault" (card #67, `Decisions/Vault name is cirBTC Vault 2026-09-19`) would be a
# false claim about a testnet fixture. Set it in the Arc mainnet build's own env, once that
# deployment exists — not here.

VITE_RPC_URL=https://sepolia.base.org
VITE_CHAIN_ID=84532
VITE_VAULT_ADDRESSES=0xb940d71b0d695e2ba2b5853bf565c69daa3e3c98

# VITE_V3_FACTORY — the deposit/exit size-impact notice's (#183) one piece of config: a Uniswap
# v3 factory address, used only to resolve the vault's basket asset / USDC pool live via
# `getPool` (never to name the pool itself, and never to compute the edge it walks — see
# chain-actions.ts's readPoolSizeImpactInputs). LEFT UNSET HERE ON PURPOSE: Base Sepolia has no
# cirBTC pool at all, so there is nothing true to fill in, and the notice correctly renders its
# qualitative-only state without one. Set this in the Arc build environment once contracts/config/
# arc-mainnet.json records a verified Arc factory address for this workspace to read — see that
# file's own `routerNote` for the factory this repository has already verified on Arc.
# VITE_V3_FACTORY=
